<title>USA: U.S. exporters report barley sold to Saudi Arabia.</title>
<headline>U.S. exporters report barley sold to Saudi Arabia.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Agriculture Department said Thursday private exporters reported sales of 110,000 tonnes of barley to Saudi Arabia for delivery during the 1997/98 marketing year.</p>
<p>The marketing year for barley began June 1.</p>
<p>Exporters must report to USDA sales of 100,000 tonnes or more of one commodity made in one day to a single destination by 1500 ET the next business day after the sale.</p>
<p>Sales of lesser quantities must be reported weekly.</p>
<p>((Washington commodities desk, 202 898 8394))</p>
</text>
